# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. The key never enters the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party and private documents.
#
# The README reports benchmarks against a device manual, an internal strategy
# document and an inspection spreadsheet. Those documents belong to their
# owners, contain named individuals, and are NOT redistributable. Only the
# aggregate scores are published. Keep them out of the repository.
#
# The publishable half of the benchmark is the INVENTED corpus (benchmarks/corpus*.txt
# and its question sets), which is force-included below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
benchmarks/manual.txt
benchmarks/hospital.txt
benchmarks/site.txt
benchmarks/manual_questions.json
benchmarks/hospital_questions.json
benchmarks/site_questions.json
benchmarks/result_*manual*
benchmarks/result_*hospital*
benchmarks/result_*site*
benchmarks/bisect_hospital/
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.doc

!benchmarks/corpus.txt
!benchmarks/corpus_en.txt
!benchmarks/corpus_es.txt
!benchmarks/questions.json
!benchmarks/questions_en.json
!benchmarks/questions_es.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derivable data. Reproduced by the download/prepare scripts; carrying it in
# the repository has no value and would make the repository unusable in size.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.bz2
*.bin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Models and weights. The trained core is ~193 MB with optimizer state; the
# downloaded engines are gigabytes. The registry records WHICH version was
# chosen and why, and that file does belong in the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
models/
!models/registry.json
*.pt
*.gguf
*.safetensors
# A downloaded pre-built engine, at the repository root. Anchored with a
# leading slash: unanchored, this rule also swallowed src/lmm/core, which is
# the package's own substrate.
/core/

# llama.cpp: the GGUF convert/quantize toolchain. A clone — derived, not committed.
llama.cpp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output. Memory files, evidence indexes and conversation logs are
# produced by running the system; several contain verbatim user input.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.lmm
*.evidence
memory.json
*.json.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.claude/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal archive. The design notes, experiment logs and research maps this
# project was built from are kept on disk but not published: they are written
# in the author's own language, they record dead ends and half-decisions rather
# than the system as it stands, and several name private material. The
# published architecture note is docs/architecture.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/internal/
notebooks/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Field trial documents: fetched from the public internet by
# benchmarks/field/fetch_documents.py, never committed. The script (URLs +
# licences) and the report are what belong in git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
benchmarks/field/documents/
benchmarks/field/work/
# Derived from those documents by `measure.py` — a graph of a document is the
# document, so it is no more redistributable than the document is. The QUESTION
# SETS are committed; the graphs and the per-sample results are not.
benchmarks/field/graphs/
benchmarks/field/results/
